==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|get with the programme}} {{qualifier|UK}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-get with the program.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|get<,,got> with the program|past_ptc2=gotten with the program|head=[[get with]] [[the]] [[program]]}}

# {{lb|en|US|idiomatic|informal}} To become [[organized]], current, or aware.
#: {{ux|en|When the student was behind on his vocabulary, the teacher said, "get with the program!"}}
# {{lb|en|US|idiomatic|informal}} To work productively toward the objective of a shared enterprise, especially after the objective or the environment has changed.
#: {{ux|en|Though natural gas prices dropped, the folks doing solar didn't '''get with the program'''.}}
# {{lb|en|US|idiomatic|informal}} To comply with the norms of a social group, especially a shared enterprise.
#: {{ux|en|Dude, '''get with the program'''! We don't do casual Fridays any more.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|become aware}} {{l|en|get a clue}}
* {{sense|become organized}} be [[on top of]] things
* get/be [[on the same page]]

